  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_93898d6e2a2e4b9e97b6d25ebc198345",
      "statement": "Brijio tab targeting is per-call and stateless: the agent passes tabId on each tool invocation, and there is no hidden selected-tab session state. When tabId is omitted, tools fall back to the active foreground tab via chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }). No select_tab session-level default is introduced.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0060-explicit-tab-listing-and-selection.md#L93-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a121545780401e0078019f68b2ac555f70072847ed49c5f602febcd56857328:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0062-thread-tabid-through-action-stack.md#L48-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36e2c9ba8d96145639bb187a00e70749e993f1a8655390732162852527832380:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e27d085f7a14900af8d185660f57b64",
      "statement": "The recommended multi-tab workflow is: list_tabs to discover tabs, choose a tabId, pass that tabId into subsequent read/action/batch/navigation calls, keep the same tabId until an intentional switch, and re-read page context (read_current_page with tabId) after navigation or any DOM mutation because element IDs are ephemeral and expire on page changes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/skills/navigation/SKILL.md#L46-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e88d87090fafbdccad1100a90f9d8ad617d8109ca840c3969042b6798fc258ce:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/skills/using-brijio/SKILL.md#L160-L201",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8eb2e1bc96f97a7d7a1dea9da751d60071febfba0a1f0be0c80b15a17980ec68:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4dc2251a5a1d44a399c5a49ea143ee00",
      "statement": "list_tabs returns a TabInfo per eligible tab with fields tabId (string), windowId (string), title, url, active (boolean), and supported (boolean). The extension queries all tabs across all windows and filters to regular HTTP/HTTPS pages using isRegularPageUrl(), excluding chrome://, chrome-extension://, about:, file://, safari://, and incognito tabs. tabId values are raw browser integers exposed as strings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0060-explicit-tab-listing-and-selection.md#L117-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa1074ba2f949e27573113f5fac5ee47c48f2f42c354239ecf569c361696124b:"
